in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @mirror/loss

# @mirror/loss/transparency — the canonical loss carrier sub-glass.
#
# THE FIRST SPECIES under @mirror/loss. Lifts the substrate's floor
# declaration `transparency(p)` from `shards/glass.mirror` into the
# loss family at the mirror altitude. NO new type — the carrier IS
# the floor declaration; this shard names the family placement.
#
# Per `glass.mirror`'s floor declaration (lines 90-95):
#
#   # transparency(p) — located opacity over property p. The substrate's
#   # loss carrier. Replaces the dead MirrorLoss scalar.
#   type transparency(p) =
#     | success
#     | partial(opacity_map)
#     | failure(opacity_map)
#
# The substrate's primary loss vocabulary. What every other
# `@mirror/loss/*` sub-glass lifts into when composing into the
# parent imperfect's L slot. The Fail-dominates / Partial-min-
# confidence / Pass-neutral algebra (per `properties-on-glass.md`'s
# transparency-monoid spec).
#
# === The lens-into-loss reading ===
#
# Per the family-root recognition (glass IS lens at three altitudes):
# this sub-glass IS a lens INTO the substrate's loss space at the
# transparency-carrier altitude. The lens projects the substrate's
# running imperfect's `L` slot when `L = transparency<p>` into the
# located-opacity-map shape; the projection preserves the
# Transparency<P> monoid; the substrate's running transparency state
# composes through this lens without dual-state divergence.
#
# Two sub-glasses observing the same imperfect MUST agree on the
# transparency total. `@mirror/loss/transparency` IS the canonical
# observer; other sub-glasses (shannon when it lands; dirichlet
# when it lands) MUST lift their scalar / energy / Massey-class
# outputs into a transparency-equivalent before composing into
# the parent imperfect. The transparency sub-glass IS the
# composition centre of the family (per the floor declaration's
# "the substrate's loss carrier" framing).
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# No new type; no new action; no new property. The carrier IS the
# floor declaration. This shard:
#
#   1. Lifts the family placement (the transparency carrier IS now
#      a named species under `@mirror/loss`).
#   2. Names the lens-into-loss reading at the family altitude (the
#      glass-IS-lens recognition realised at the first species).
#   3. Re-exports the floor carrier (`out transparency`) so consumers
#      pulling `in @mirror/loss/transparency` get the named type.
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (23rd instance):
# the substrate already had `transparency`; this shard does not
# re-declare; it names. Per
# [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]: `transparency` is
# substrate vocabulary already; the shard at the loss-family altitude
# IS a re-export-with-family-placement, not a re-declaration.
#
# === Why this lands first ===
#
# The brief proposed four sub-glasses; only transparency lands this
# tick. The reasons:
#
#   - transparency is the substrate's primary loss carrier; every
#     other measurement composes through it. Landing it first
#     anchors the family.
#   - transparency already exists at the floor; the lift is
#     substrate-pull-only (no new declaration; pure family
#     placement).
#   - shannon / dirichlet / massey each require a consumer pull
#     before their L-slot semantics resolve cleanly:
#       * shannon needs a consumer for the scalar-additive monoid
#         (waiting for `glass.mirror`'s opacity.weight to be lifted).
#       * dirichlet needs the sheaf-diffusion Houdini fixpoint to
#         land (waiting for `@mirror/homotopy/A_infinity` pull).
#       * massey needs `@mirror/homotopy/massey` to pull (per the
#         prophecy insight's cascade order).
#   - Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]: substrate-pull discipline
#     forbids declaring forward-promised types where the consumer
#     hasn't pulled yet. The family root + transparency anchor IS
#     the next tick; the rest interleave with consumer pulls.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/transparency.md (the floor declaration;
#               the L-slot monoid laws),
#               docs/specs/mosaic-as-type-system.md §2 (the imperfect-
#               as-monad floor; transparency IS the L slot's primary
#               instance),
#               docs/specs/properties-on-glass.md (the transparency-
#               on-glass discipline; properties carry transparencies
#               per the cross-language verification surface).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (transparency IS substrate vocabulary; this
#                      shard names the family placement, not the
#                      type),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                      lift IS family placement; the carrier stays
#                      at the floor; the placement happens at the
#                      mirror altitude).
# Substrate recognitions: [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the 23rd-instance recognition realised at the
#                      first species; transparency was already the
#                      carrier),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull]] (no invention; the
#                      shard is family-placement-only),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (transparency<p> is
#                      parametric on the property; the L slot stays
#                      typed).
# Related shards: glass.mirror (the floor declaration of
#                 transparency<p>; this shard re-exports without
#                 re-declaring),
#                 mirror/loss.mirror (the family root; this shard
#                 IS the first species under it).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/mirror/loss/transparency.mirror` declares
# `@mirror/loss/transparency` as a species under the `@mirror/loss`
# family.

prism @mirror/loss/transparency {
  focus transparency
  project transparency
  split transparency
  shift transparency
  settle transparency
}

# Re-export the floor carrier under the family placement. The
# carrier IS `transparency<p>` declared at `shards/glass.mirror`
# lines 92-95; pulled into scope through `in @glass` above.
#
# Consumers pulling `in @mirror/loss/transparency` get the carrier
# named at the family altitude:
#
#   in @mirror/loss/transparency  --  the family-altitude pull
#   in @glass                      --  the floor-altitude pull
#
# Both yield the same type. The family-altitude pull additionally
# enrols the consumer in the loss-family composition discipline
# (other @mirror/loss sub-glasses MUST lift into this carrier before
# composing into the parent imperfect's L slot).
out transparency

out @mirror/loss/transparency
